The Parliament does not support an amendment providing Tymoshenko’s freedom
Today the Parliament of Ukraine in the course of amendments to the Criminal Procedural code rejected an attempt to repeal an article according to which the leader of the Opopt, Yulia Tymoshenko, was convicted.
The amendment, which would result in the releasing former prime minister ' s imprisonment, had been defused during a second reading of a bill to commute sentences for economic offenses.
Tymoshenko was Sentenced to Seven Years in prison for signing a gas deal with Russia that was deemed unfavourable.
Judgments have not yet been final; the court will consider Tymoshenko's appeal in December.
Tymoshenko argues that the veripulation is the political retaliation of the regime; in the West the process was also suspected of being biased.
The proposal to repeal Article 365 of the Code of Criminal Procedure, according to which the former prime minister had been convicted, was supported by 147 members of Parliament.
To ratify it would take 226 votes.
