Iranian students are ready to die for their country's nuclear program.
They've created a human shovel.
Hundundrate Hundreds of university students have created a human shield around a nuclear power plant in Iran.
Thus, they want to express their support for their country's nuclear program in the face of a possible Israeli attack.
On Tuesday at no a no-hundred afternoon, prayers of the students in front of entering the building was followed by a melody of both the U.S. and Israel.
In Isfahan, Iran, several hundred university students have created a human shirk around the Isfahan Uranium Engrafting Plant.
