"to limit the influence of some groups of people who tend to influence the disciplinary and appellate council, which leads to disgusting situations," Patslick said. He does not hide his antipity, for example, Sparta's director Daniel Krzhetinsky.
One of his priorities will be to strengthen the relationship between FAČR and the Czech Olympian Committee, with whose help he will lobby at the highest political level to allocate more money for sports from lottery training.
