Hamburg
For German citizens, the situation is understandable. According to one study, 84% of Germans consider it unacceptable that banks speculate on agricultural products, such as wheat and corn.
The two-thirds of the respondents are demanding that Deutsche Bank and other banks stop trade in agricultural products, as trade exacerbates the problems faced by the poorest people around the world.
Concludions were given in a study conducted by the Institute of Social Research and Statistical Analysis of Forsa on behalf of Foodwatch consumer organization.
