Referring to Deutsche Bahn’s internal anti-crisis plan, the Bild Newspaper reports that an investment with a total of about 300 million euros are planned until 2015.
The investments are designed to increase the efficiency of locomotives and the railway network even in extreme weather conditions.
The number of own and attracted employees, involved in the removal of snow from tracks and platforms, will be halved, to 16 000.
The goal is to clear the platforms from snow and ice before the start of work and 90 percent of the required arrows for a period of four-to-five hours.
