“Beauty and sorrow” has wove together the experience of the war years more or less unremarkable men and women, on both sides of the front line, from schoolchildren and botanist scientists to mountaineers, doctors, ambulance drivers and employees.
Some of these people will become heroes.
Someone will fall in captivity, will lose a hand or a leg, go crazy or will die.
Their lives froze here like church suppositories: the new ones are added to a variety of others, and some at this time are extinguished.
Mr. Englund's book is a departure from the standard of historical books.
