“Beauty and sorrow” traces the fate of such people as Florence Farmbroo, an English nursing nurse in the Russian army, and Reichard Sturpf, a young sailor of the German fleet of the high sea.
Their stories are taken mainly from memoirs, letters and other already published materials.
