In addition, there may be a general recalculation of votes in all urns in elections when there is a sign that there is a sign that there is a difference between the intended candidate-winner of the elections in question and those who received the second place in the vote is less than one percentage, provided that at the beginning of the session there is a request from the representative of the party and/or the coalition that exposed the second of the above-mentioned candidates.
A general recalculation of the votes will also be made, if at the end of the usual count it is established that there is a difference between the vibrator and a second-place candidate less than one percent, provided that there is an application from a political party whose candidate took a second place, in the event that ballot boxes that have been taken into account at a partial recostification.
It is worth noting that in this situation there are elections in Moreligia, where, according to APPR, the difference between the first and the second place is only 0.16 percent, not even counting 129 votes out of a total of 923 protocol.
