Quintet included the country on the tour in honor of the twenty-anniversary of his quarrel
A trip to Costa Rica is a dream come true
In an exclusive interview with Viva bassist Jeff Ament from Pearl Jam said the band was ready to give one of the best concerts next Sunday at the National Stadium.
There was more than 20 years of expectation, but the group says that for them it is also a dream, which has become a reality - to play in this country.
This was the statement of basbist and the founder, Jeff Ament, who gave an exclusive interview to Viva from Brazil last week.
The group is located on the territory of South America as part as part as part of a tour in honor of the twentieth anniversary of the work of the work and on Sunday, 20, will make its only stop in Central America.
On this day they will perform at the National Stadium, starting at 7:30 p.m., together with a team from Los Angeles The X and the local group Las Robertas.
This is an outburst from a conversation, the complete decoding of which is available online in The Nation.
For your Costa Rican fans it’s like Pearl Jam to play in Costa Rica? Do you know what your fans are experiencing?
A trip to Costa Rica is a dream come true for us as well.
It’s only our second visit to the South and Central America, so far everything’s going well.
I’ve only been in Costa Rica once – on a vacation, it’s a beautiful country, and I think that we can stay there for a few days.
Therefore, we are very happy to bring our music there.
I'm questioning it because there's some devotion to the band; the fans live in suspense in the days before a concert.
What will you say to your most loyal fans?
Thank you for having been with us all these years.
It took us almost 21 years to get to Costa Rick, thank you for waiting so long, and we’re deplorable that it took so much time to get here.
Some people, in anticipation of your concert, treat him like the biggest show of the year.
Does this add a bit of tension to your visit?
Some of the biggest shows we’ve played over the past 21 years have taken place over the last two weeks.
“We’ve held some great shows in São Paulo and we hope this brings us into a uniform for this concert in Costa Rica.
In fact, we really want to play here.
We love this country, we love to surf and jungle, as for these two things, Costa Rika - one of the best countries in the country in the world.
How did you learn about Costa Rica and its serfeing waves?
We have a lot of sulfur friends, and I have a good friend who lives in Tamarindo and the waves here are unparalleled.
My friends are always surfing in Costa Rica and Nicaragua, as well as in Mexica, it’s an excellent place for surfing, that’s how we’ve learned about it, from people who love to serfing.
Looking at the tour, we can say that you have made a grandiose show with a lot of songs.
What do you plan to perform in Costa Rica?
Since we've never played there before, we don't have any restrictions on what we can do.
We will try to make the best show possible with a wide variety of songs; we will try to play a few songs from each album and to present to our fans a wide variety of repertoire.
You'll never repeat your repertoire.
How's it gonna work?
I think it’s kind of because we have nine records and we can play more than 120 songs, and everyone likes different songs, so it’s hard to choose which songs to play every night.
When there are two or three songs that we haven’t played for a while, it keeps us in tone and surprises us because it reminds us of the reasons why we’ve loved these songs and what we might have forgotten.
This makes the show more interesting for us and so I think it makes it more interesting for people.
With this tour, you are celebrating 20 years of your career.
Looking back, it’s hard to believe what you’ve done?
Yeah, of course.
In the first place, I think that none of us could ever imagine that we will be in a rock band and that we've been doing this for more than 20 years make it look like a dream.
We rejoice in our luck and we are very excited that we can continue to create music together.
We all love each other and we love making music.
We are happy to go to the place in the world where we always wanted to go.
Everything is very good for us.
What does it means for you to be a significant part of granage’s helm?
It has always been an honor to be part of this group of great collectives.
We are good friends with guys from Soundgarden, Mudhoney and Alice in Chains
It’s great when the movement grows from a group of friends, and it’s unusual.
From time to time there is one group from the same city, but much more strange, when five or ten groups appear at the same time in the same city.
We are delighted and it's an honor to be part of the Seattle group.
I’m still playing with some of them from time to time.
Last year, we were at Alice in Chains festival and we were in Canada with Mudhoney, we’ve seen Soundgarden during their tour, so we’re delighted to be friends with all of them and it’s an honor for us to be a part of Seathetla’s sound that turned out.
It is also very strange that a group like yours stays together in the same line-up for such a long time.
Yes, four of us have been together for 21 years, and Matt (Camerón) joined us 13 years ago, which in itself is much longer than many bands exist.
Firstly, I think we are lucky that we are still alive, and secondly, we take care of others.
We are all very close friends and, thanks to this, musical roads were also opened, which give everyone freedom of experiment.
We are trusting each other’s music and it couldn’t be any better.
Your relation to the word of fame was not easy; but thanks to your success you were able to do everything that you wanted.
How do you find the balance?
When we grew, it became easier to find a balance.
We take care about not being on tour for too long, because it's easy to get into this game of big crowds and people who love your music.
While you remember that the people are here for the sake of music, it reminds you that you have to respect the music and what it has done, not deciding to be famous and to be a rock-and-mother, something that none of us really care about.
How do you remember your other, Manother Love Bone?
I think we’re going to write really good songs and at the beginning it was gorgeous.
We've been a band for almost three years and haven't released an album until Andrey Wows died.
There were a lot of frustration, because it lasted so long, and the most important thing is that we are still close friends with Bruce (Ferweather) and Greg (Gilmore), who began with us in a band, and when I heard a song or see a photo, I think about the incredible person who was Andy, and how he forced me to laugh, it has always been a pleasure to go for a job, to laugh, to talk about music.
It was a wonderful person, and we miss him.
Las Robertas will be responsible for the Costa Rica.
It’s true that you’re familiar with her work, especially Eddie Vedder, and so you’ve picked her to be discovered?
“Yeah don’t send us some video offers, and it’s been a band that we’ve liked most of everyone, so we can’t wait to see what Las Robertas can offer live, and this should be very exciting.
Why do you constantly change words in Yellow Ledbetter at concerts?
It’s a question for Ed (Eddie Vedder), so I don't know.
He sings it, and I think he uses the first thing that comes to his mind.
Who affected you as a bass player?
There's so many of them.
Among the first to come to my mind is Geezer Butler, John Entwistle, C.J. Ramon, John Doe, Paul McCartney, Chuck Dukowski ...
There are so many of them that I can talk all day about bassists I love.
How did Pearl Jam achieve success in maintaining the relevance of grange, despite the fact that it is no longer in vogue?
I don't think we all can feel some detachment from the word grunge.
When I’m thinking of him, he reminds me of the bands I’ve mentioned earlier like Mudhoney, Soundgarden, Nirvana and everyone who showed up at the Same time, and if it’s important now, I think it’s wonderful because it’s a music worth listening, and teams like Mudhoney now create music better than ever.
Initially, your music was glorious, and now it has become more positive.
How do you Explain This Modification?
It’s interesting, as I think there are a few songs in the album that may seem easier, but there are songs like The End or Just Breathe that are considered very globt, although they may sound a little positive.
From both, when Ed played them, I crippled when I listened to them, those songs very gloating.
I think that when you’re growing up and there’s been an injury in your life and you’ve lost a member of a family or a friend, these events begin to influence your creativity and your music, and these two songs, of course, refurbish it for me.
So, I think that you can be a happieged person and still be able to create gloomy music.
Peru :
Fuchimori was again hospitalized for medical screening
Ex-president Alberto Fuchimori was hospitalized on Tuesday in a public hospital, for examination for loss of musculoskeletal strength that is observed in the legs, said his family doctor.
Fuhimori, who has been sentenced to 25 years in prison for human rights irregularities (1990-2000), suffers from several diseases, including language cancer, because of which he was operated four times and is monitored.
Undersecretary Alejandro Aginaga, who is his personal physician, told television channel N that Fuchimori will be examined for three days at the National Institute of Neopplastic Illness to estimate the cause and loss of force in his lower extremities.
Aginaga said that, in his opinion, Fouhimori should be a candidate to receive the benefit of pardon for humanitarian reasons; however, he said that he does not want it because he knows that he is innocent.
He underwent four linguation of lung cancer, weighed 18 kilograms, which included other diseases, such as severe erosive gastritis cysts of the pancreas, kidney cysts, kidney stones, high blood pressure and problems with circuliquence in the legs.
Fuhoimori has been in prison since September 2007, at the National Special Operations Police Office.
In April 2009, he was sentenced to 25 years in prison for the killing of 25 people by a detachment of an extinguishing army, which acted secretly in the first years of his reign.
Muhika goes to Mexica to strengthen political ties
An official delegation led by Urugua President Jose Muhikoi, consisting of several ministers and businessmen, will visit Mexico on Tuesday to expand trade between the two countries and to start negotiations on the political problems of the region.
Mujica will meet next Wednesday with his Mexican colleague, Felipe Calderón, the most important point of an extensive plan of meetings with the political, commercial authorities and meetings with the community of Uruguayans living in Mexico, according to a schedule published by the leadership of the Urugua.
The meeting between the two presidents in Guadalajara will be “favourable for the exchange of information on the political relationship between the two nations,” according to the leadership of the South American country on its website.
According to local media, Mujica is pushing Calderon’s support for Hugura in an incident with France that happened when French President Nikolay Sarkozy put the South American country on tax harbour sheet at the G20 meeting in the French city of Cannes.
Sarkozy in his speech jeopardized from the international community those countries that remain tax galvans, a statement that provoked a prophygooted UUGU swarm and a review for the advice of its ambassador in a European country.
Mexico has presided the G20 since November, a group set out of the most heavily developed and developing countries, and has, in fact, an exchange of tax information agreement with the South American country since January this year to avoid double taxation.
In recent years, the government of Uruguay has tried in recent years to expedite the conclusion of tax-examination agreements in order to leave this “gray list” of the Organization for Economic Co-Cooperation and Development, compiled from countries that don’t use international standards of tax cooperation.
With regard to the trade plan, the Free Trade Complementary Trade Agreement (STS), which has increased the trade turnover between the two countries since 2004.
Cotted plumber will become a three-piece with "Super Mario 3D Land"
Super Mario fought tirelessly for more than 25 years to save Princess Peach from Boweser’s evil paws, but he has never done so before in three dimensions: in the “Super Mario 3D Land”, he will fight for the girl’s love in stereoscopic technology.
The publication, which will be available in stores around the world this month, was created taking into account the characteristics of the Nintendo 3DS portable console, which allows you to play in the three dimensions without the need to use glasses.
"Mario is a hero who has to tell you how a stereoscopy without glasses will work," Nimentendo's press office in Spain, Omar Alvarez, said during the presentation of the game in Madrid.
Alvarez said "Super Mario 3D Land" is "Nintendo's first video game, specially designed for this platform", because so far successful products like "Star Fox 64 3D" or "Zelda: Ocarina of Time 3D" were adaptations of existing games.
Nyntendo spokeswoman said that, despite its existence in 3D, "Super Mario 3D Land" is an "accessible" video game that allows you to enjoy a fast and movable game.
Álvarez said "Super Mario 3D Land" contains two games in the same line: the first is "simplified", to attract less experienced users.
Once started, the majority of the experts will go “in the second circle” to the level of the game, which this time are more complex.
In addition, users are able to choose in real-time between “D aggressive” or something that only influences the depth of the action, but which you need to play in three dimensions in order to overcome a variety of hurdles and “not succumb to optical illusions”.
This Intrusion of Super Mario in the Three Dimensions also marks the return of the hero to a portable console, which hasn’t happened since 2005.
In this game, Nintendo winks fans of the series and repeates a successful formula from previous games, the plumber with the mustache needs to pass through the dangerous gummappened platforms to liberate Princess Peach.
However, the player will detect new movements, scenery, costumes and enemies, as well as “playing” Luigi.
Colum guarantees the dismantling of Portillo to the United States
President Álvaro Kolom said on Tuesday that Alfonso Porillo’s extradition proceedings had begun to respond in the U.S. for languishing $70 million.
Thus ends the process by which Guatemala responded to the request of the northern country, which demanded the extradition of Portillo in order to be judged.
At the press conference, Kolom said that his decision relates to the independence of the forensic and executive authorities, taking into account that the court of first instance has already signed an extradition.
He claimed that during his mandate, he did not “give your hands” to legal decisions and took all the extradition procedures that he had ever aware of.
Along with Portillo, Sercio Ruano Marroquin will be extradited for murder and grievous bodily injuries, as well as Edgar Estrada Morales and Victor Estrada Paredes, both for selling drugs.
What Kolom was done shows the executive process after all legal and constitutional courts have been exhausted in order to proclamate the former head of the state from 2000 to 2004.
In accordance with the decisions of the Fifteenth of the Criminal Court and the Constitutional Court (COP), Portillo will be extradited once with a decision on his legal status in Guatemal and a guarantee of his human human rights.
Portillo was found presiduced to embezzlement Q120 million in the Ministry of Defense during the presidential term, which was a pre-extradition process, but the Ministry of Public Relations filed an appeal and rediscovered the case.
Trinijove helped 6,000 young at-to-feed people at risk
The organization was created to prevent the marginalization of young people without an upbringing
Trinijove’s results of the first 25-year-affiliated social support organization are important: 6,000 young people suscepted about social isolation have helped overcome difficult situations during this quarter of a century.
To this it is necessary to add more than a hundred jobs created for this social group.
Anniversary served as an occasion for the results of the ceremony held in the premises of the old Fabra I Coats, where more than 300 people came.
Trinjove was born next to Trinitat Vella in 1986 to help young people with a lack of education, lack of work and problems with drugs or pronounced marginalization.
Yesterday’s celebration at Sant Andreu brings together a large number of responsible organizations and institutions, which in these 25 years have collaborated with an association.
A different political representation during the elections showed a single character of the work done by Trinijove.
After the Chairman of the Generalitat, Artur Mase and his predecessor Khordi Pukhol, the ceremony was attended by an ex-consultant of the Socialist education, Ernest Maragal, and the ex-Lieutenant of the mayor and the Current Eco-Prosocialist, a member of the municipal council of Ricard Goma.
Also appeared in Fabra I Coats the Current Social Welfare and Family Constitutant, Josep Lewis Clereris and the Social Work of La Cahica, Haume Lanaspa.
He said that Trinijove was graduated at a very difficult time and that the current period is also difficult, but he added that the work done so far “is a good base”.
The Chairman cited Trinijove as an example of the struggle against bad circumstances and the settlement of hopes for people who are experiencing difficulties.
“The Crisis isn’t new for the organization and work done to her,” he said.
Captured building, where mass parties were organized, was evacuated
Invailators occupied 11 of the 13 floors of the building on Balsemes street, 51
12 occupiers left the building yesterday at no-leaf
It seems that the nightmare, experienced by the neighbors living in house 51 on Balmes street, has come to an end.
Twelve people yesterday at noon voluntarily left the building, which they illegally occupied and where they organized mass parties that irritated their neighbors by a court decision without the intervention of the police.
When the operation was completed, the lock on the door was exchanged to prevent a recurrence of the situation.
“From this moment there will be pass control here”, – said the manager.
Skwatters, which ousted 11 of the 13 floors of the building, the rest are inhabited, embezzled all the electricity and part of the water, painted the walls and left traces of all sorts, especially javages of alcoholic beverages.
The first three floors were a platform for mass parties, which lasted up to two days and irritated the owners.
Immediately after the building is a nightclub, Balmes 51, which also suffered damage.
The owner, Maria Pantina, told Europa Press that its income has decreased by 80% since the building was occupied.
The owner of the club says that the invaders of the building dragged her into an unfair competition, since they were selling drinks for three euros, while in the club for 10.
In addition, the owner of the disco had to respond to the complaints of the neighbors to the noise, although, as she noted, the noise was caused not by the visitors of the club, but by the residents of squandering and, first of all, by those who visited the parties who organized, the frequency and intensity of which increased, as the angry neighbors said.
The owner of the club said that the inconvenience was so large that it even reached an agreement with the owner of the property, and for nine months as he “forgives” the payment of the loan.
The city police also confirmed that in recent recent weeks received more complaints from their neighbors about the situation.
PP, Advisor to Alberto Fernánd Diaz, said last week “immediately evaporates a building to address the problems of coexistence and the common spirit of its neighbors and derogation in this area”.
The popular leader explained that until the summer only one floor of the building was occupyed, but in the last few months squotters have invaded all the floors and almost every room and that in some of them burglations occurred.
In this sense, he added that “we need to put an end to Impunacid and steadfaciatedly resist the unscrupulous work in the building.”
Yesterday, police officers evacuated the building in Nou Barris.
At about 15:30, the police went to Montral, 35 after receiving a bell from a neighbour who noticed how four people entered the building.
Four were arrested immediately.
A park or a mountain?
The architects agreed with the possibility of the competition after anzruption of contributions
The municipal competition for 16 doors resumed the debate on the role of Kolesrola in Barcelona
In the mid-80s, on the ascent of the now extinguished Corporation of Barcologna (SKB), this administration printed promotional flip-floages for Kohlisola.
The booklet described the mountain as a large park of the capital's of Barcelona.
What’s more, this was accompanied by a comparison in the images with Central Park of New York.
With the death of SKB, in 1987, the park regained a place in the consciousness of many as the highest point of Barcelona as the capital of Catalonia, one of the few who are oriented not to the north-south, but up (mountain) - down (sea).
Positioning Kolserola as a natural park contradicts this idea.
Proto-type was not Central Park, but Yellowwton, with a wild boar as the Yogi bear.
This was the case, so, in September, the council did not announce a huge competition, consisting of 16 competitions for many other goals in Kolesrola.
By the gate refers to the idea of the park, of course.
Either this way, or someone wants to put the gates on the field.
The question stands alone: Kolesrola? the park or the mountain?
Conveniments, and their organizational side, and their impact on the city, are a topic to discuss all architects of Barcelona.
It’s almost the most repetitive topic, discussed when two members of this cranberic clan, recognize each other in an elevator.
And this fact leads precisely to one of the few coincidences between what three architects of Barcelona and the scientists who were present said.
Miguel Roldand, Daniel Modolo and Mara Bayona: the competition is appropriate
For Roldan, after reaching the coastline becomes “necessary” to discuss the “forward side of the mountain”, when Ildepon Serda’s proposal, a mountain with green apples, was not carried out.
“It should be assumed that Barcelona’s largest park is the beach.
Among other things, due to its excellent accessibility.
Kohlserola is more complex,” says the architect, for whom the headline of the “Kolserola gate” contains a “verbal trap”: we don’t have to think about them “like the entrance to the park, but as a restriction of certain areas where we have to act.”
Modolo, like Roldan and Bayon with experience in urban construction, called the proposal an “intelligence task” with “some hazards”.
The risks arising in view of the “uncertificate prediction of the public space” after the experience of the 80s, which ended at the forum “its swan sing”.
The first fascination is the actual limitation of the boundaries, where you can build.
Residivizing something is the preparation of the next step,” it’s the transition.
“We need to think about new urban planning tools, because the current [conciliation to the Secretary-General’s General Plan (GSP)] can lead to real misfortune.”
Closer to the matter, Modolo believes that simplification of Kolserola valley "can be understood as a park, Barcelona, and not" as a purely topographical issue.
Modolo recalls that there is already a work done outside of Calcerola, which is “should not be allowed by”, although he is thankful for the opportunity that the mayor’s office offers his profession, to join this project “from the very beginning”.
Moreover, it understands that the proximity of the mountain towards the city is a pass, which allows architects to enter into a debate, but “he doubts” whether this technical profile is something that should lead interdisciplinary teams (“success”, he argues), which was supposed to create: “Architectors should only be an instrument”.
Bayon hints that the answer to the question that sets the name of this part is complex, since there is a lack of a general appearance of Kolserola in the rules of the competition: "There were 16 intersecting competitions announced," he says, "in the meaning of the sea-mountain, but there is no longitudinal reading here to see and understand the area as a whole."
This causes, at least in its case, to decide for the participation of 16 competitions.
On the other hand, the project for some gate can intersect according to the program and the design of an architectural project for the neighboring gate.
From your point of view, advice should be ensured that the lane directly over Ronda de Dalt should provide in its entirety an area equipped to create a smooth transition between the city and the green.
