Minister Dionicio Pérez Hakomet talks about the details of the disaster where the Minister of the Interior, Francisco Blake, and seven other people were killed.
The Ministry of Liaison and Sanitation (IC) reported that the results obtained on an unfortunate accident that killed Interior Minister Franísco Blake Mora and seven others, showed that the helicopter hit directly the ground in a state of complete incorporation, without trying to make an emergency landing.
During a press conference, Dénicio Pérez Hamome, the Minister of Communications and Transport, said that before the aircraft rose up, the pilot found out that the weather conditions were suitable for the flight.
Elements, which seem to show that the ship has had several contacts with the ground, wings came into contact with the Trees at 25 meters, where the tool lost a flusery.”
He also reported that the vessel was destined for 19 people, respectively, it complied with the necessary requirements for the transportation of people.
He also said that the studies carried out in the area of the impact did not indicate the presence of parts on the ground.
“The study reports that in another place there are no components of the vessel, the impact occurred in a state of structural intelivity.
“Heavard was intended for 19 passengers, which satisfactorily met the requirements of passenger transportation.
The land in this place has a slope from seven to 30 degrees.
At the moment, said the Secretary, the most important thing is to obtain the results as soon as possible; however, the study can take several months or even one year.
In the meantime, Gilberto López Meyer, the general director of airports and Auxiliary services, he said that during the strike the presidential helicopter was controlled at cruising velocity and that this happened on a soft rising ground.
"This information strengthens the hypothesization of the usual flight manoeuvre at the time of the strike," he said.
At the press-conference, the owner of SCT, Perez Hakomet, listed six important elements in the investigation:
Visual flight:
According to the rules of the aviation, the flight was carried out according to the rules of visual flight, which means that the team should have visibility during the flight and landing.
Weather conditions:
AICM’s reports revealed suitable conditions for take-off, when the aircraft went to the border area between the city of Mejiko and the state of Mexica, where layers of clouds were observed at low altitudes.
Selected routes:
It is possible that due to the conditions of cloudability, the team was looking for a zone of lower height and greater visibility in the Kuernavaca valley.
Scate of impact.
Coordinates of the impact and the last recording from the radar of the aircraft coincide, probably before the impact there was no loss of control or change of the direction of the flight.
Scattered wretched in a small area:
The information available so far indicates that the blow fell on the front and lateral lines.
The scattering of the wreckage makes it clear that the helicopter collided with the ground under structural incorporation.
Proluminous signs of a fire or an explosion have been found:
Unexpected Evidential Evidence Remain in the wreckage of a ship, some kind of bang or fire.
Residual studies show that there may have been multiple contacts with the ground.
During the work on the site were found chilners of the aircraft at an altitude of 9.200 feet above sea level, the ground has a slope of seven degrees to 30 degrees.
In the pictures, a sequence is shown, in which it was collapsing along the way.
The information contains facts that seem to show that the helicopter could have had several collisions with the ground.
After a thorough examination in a larger area than an outlined area next to the place where the disaster took place, no scattered parts of the aircraft were found, which strengthens the assumption that the impact occurred under conditions of structural integral.
MASS Announces Obesity Genry Search Program
The social protection leads a study to find an obession gene in children and young people; it is supported by IPN specialists
The Mexican Social Welfare (MSSI) announced that it is conducting a study to detect an obesity gene for children and young people, which has been dubbed “Agenetic Geneticists in Child Absiveness and Adolescence”, which will provide a calculation of signs associated with being overweight.
In a statement, Miguel Cruz Lópes, the head of Biochematory Medical Research of the National Medical Center of the 21st century, explained that a multidisciplinary team from therapists, nurses, nutritionists and social workers has been collected.
This team is facilitated by specialists and graduate students of the National Institute of Health of the Natia (NIPH) and the Center for Scientific Research and Higher Education (CINVESTAV) of the National Polytechnic Institute (NPI).
In the study, the population (registered or not) is invited to take part by going to MSSI sports centers taking part in a study, where every Saturday, from 8:00 a.m. tests will be carried out with the participation of children.
He stressed that the protocol began to be carried out at a sports center in Cuautemoke (in the western state of Mehiko), and from October 8, events have been held at a sports center in Nesawalkoyotl (east of the state of Mehiko).
After the goal of attracting from 500 to 600 children is reached, the study will continue at the Attendantity Sports Center (syugo Mehiko) and, finally, at Morelos (nères Mejiko).
He Explained that the purpose of this study is to understand the components and the importance of genetics regarding the development of obession and to establish the risk factor among children and young Mexicans to prevent the occurrence of chronic degenerative diseases
On November 14, World Diabetes Day will celebrate World Diabetes Day, and the main goal is to collect three thousand children and adolescents between the ages of the age of 6 to 14 with the permission of their parents and under their supervision to complete individual meals.
They will also be asked about physical activity and the history of family hereditary diseases in order to avoid risk factors that lead to diseases such as diabetic or renal insufficiency.
He explained that anthropometracytic measurements of all participants (sweating, height and circumcilobia), the measurement of blood pressure and glucose levels, fats, cholesterol, and insufficiency and a genetic test will be carried out (to identify genes that are associated with childhood obescence).
Cruz López said this study reflects the concern of health professionals about worrying weight gains among children.
In medical studies carried out in the period from 1999 to 2006, it is said that in just six years there was an increase: in the case of boys, 77 percent were obese, in the case of girls 47%; as for excess weight, there has also been a significant increase here,” the MSSI specialist said.
He said the justification for searching for markers is based on the fact that the country's population differs from other peoples in its genetic history.
He reported that, on average, the Mexican is a 65 percent descendant of U.S. Indians, a 30 per cent discriminated against Europeans and a five-percent per cent miscondalous of Africans and this condition affected genes that are associated with diabetic and overweight.
He explained that mainly a consequence of the genetics of obesity is the inaccuracy of the body to burn the excess of the energy we consume (calories), and it is deposited in the form of fat.
The researcher explained that the direct benefit for the participants is a comprehensive assessment of children, which can determine whether they have at least a degree of excess weight or obesan.
Even, he said, the presence of dark folds on the neck (athletes) and forearms means the probability of impaired metabolism and even pre-diabetes.
Information is handled with full confidentiality, the doctors pass it in a Written to the parents to whom they explain all measurements and changes in the way of life that need to be taken to avoid the disease.
Kruz López explained that there are three main reasons for being overweight, obese, and other chronic diseases: a sedentary lifestyle, a lack of daily physical inactivity, spending most of the day at home in front of a TV, and the use of transport at a short distance instead of walking.
It also happens due to high calorie intensification, that is, an increase in the consumption of sweets and carbohydrates (thamale, bread, pizza, hamburgers, etc.) with a high content of fats and proteins and a genetic predisposition, analyzed in this program.
Asphalt UNAM will be able to avoid fiscitioners
Raphael Herrera, a researcher of UNAM Chemists, has developed a polymer-modified bitumen to produce a mixture of best quality resistant to the ambient and temporal.
If the signals sent by the road surface were paid attentivates, it would be necessary to renovate about 200 thousand pits for each season of the rains in the metropolitan area in the Valley of Mehiko, says Raphael Errera Nahera, a researcher of the Faculty of Chemistry of UNAM, and adds that if the process of building and maintaining an asphalted road surface is correct, then the number of pits can be reduced or completely reduced.
In his eliguation based on pits described in the International Year of Chemistry, it is reported that the laboratory for which he is responsible develops a polymer-modified belt for the production of a mixture with characteristics close to gnouum, but with the best resistance at both high and at low temperatures.
Errera Nahra said that this type of modified bitumen can be used in places where the weather is extremely hot, as in some cities in the north, to improve the quality of the roads and, therefore, the antipocr for the formation of pits.
He explained that bitumen, the heaviest part of the oil is a sequence of hydrocarbon molecules, some - a high molecular weight called asphalts, and others - the low molecular weight called magnates, which together give its characteristic visculoscular behavior to the road coating.
Viscous-elastic behavior of the bitumen lies in the fact that in high temperatures of about 180 degrees, it behaves like a fluid, at 120 its viscosity is very high, and at 50 degrees Celsius it maintains an almost solid state, while at very low temperatures the bitum becomes blossimile, he said.
This means that street asphalt resistance isn’t constant, but changes throughout the day, depending on the natural conditions and temperature, a specialist in chemical engineering said.
Scholar chymnaphak reminded that Mehiko streets are mostly covered with a floppy coating, which is made up of six layers of the material, of which the last three include bitum.
Among the most upper strata there is bitumen, composed of small stones lowered into the bitum and then compressed.
Each stone, which comprehends this coating, he said immersed in bat.
With the movement of the vehicles and putting the effort, this helps the forces very well to be distributed along a road surface.
If it were modified asphalt, then they would be distributed even better, said the chemical engineer.
On an asphalt coating, he added the last stratfine layer, which is called a layer of drift, which is made of small stone, in fact the sand is also immersed in asphalt.
Since this is a layer that will be in contact with transport wheels, it should have more resistance than asphalt coating and provide ground friction.
Being a part of the road surface that will receive and distribute these efforts, the depreciation layer also necessitates proper thickness and must be taken into account the material from which it is manufactured.
The weather, especially the moisturum and temperature changes, are also very important factors to consider, especially the water, he said because it significantly affects the state of asphale an asphalt.
When the ground is dreary, the water penetrates the coating and it is difficult to get out of there, this causes softening of all layers of coating and, consequently, the formation of pits.
During the formation of pits, he said that a depreciation layer wears first and only then it acts on bitumen, but the damage does not occur instantly, the process of which should be given attention at the for the first signs of ongoing repair programs.
Also, a member of the National system of researchers explained that the transport load is another important factor in the formation of holes, and therefore the thickness of each coating layer should always be associated with the transport load and it is necessary to guarantee the fulfillment of this requirement in order to prevent the frequent appearance of pits.
Raphael Herrera said that a lot still needs to be explored and, for example, bitumen emulsions, which in other countries are already on the market and even help fix pits easily and without the use of high temperatures.
What was not enough for the candidate from Vallia to become a new Miss Colombia?
Analyzing the causes that have prevented Cerne Melina Ramirez to receive the crown of Miss Colombia.
