The Northern Flote, a new gate for the entry of Russian gas to Europe.
The Nord Stream gas pipeline, connecting Western Europe and Russia directly along the bottom of the Baltic Sea, has been launched.
It is designed to supply gas to the equivalencies of 30 million households.
“Gazprom, the Russian gigantic gas maker, wanted to celebrate this event with a pump.
More than 500 guests, including four heads of state and government, took part last Tuesday on the shores of the Baltic, between the orchestra’s performance and exquisite snacks, at the opening of the Nord stream, a new gas pipeline that directly connects Russia and Germany underwater.
German Chancellor Angela Machear, Russian President Dmitry Medvedev, François Fillon and his Dutch counterpart Mart Rütte together turned the symbolic valve that monitors the flow of Russian gas to the Western European network.
On the new gas pipeline of 27.5 thousand additional cubic meter of gas will be supplied every year to Western Europe through the first pipe with a length of 1, 224 km, which connects the Leningrad region with the land of Mecklenburg Pomerania.
The second pipeline should be ready at the end of 2012, ensuring the supply of a total of 55 million cubic meter of gas, which are equivalent to the total consumption of France.
And the possibility of building a third of the pipeline in the same direction is already being negotiated.
For Gazprom in accrue the timely completion of this huge project is a victory.
The project met the fierce resistance of Poland and the Baltic states.
The Northern Stream will really allow you to deliver gas directly to Germany, avoiding passage through a third country (Poland or Ukraine).
These two countries will lose part of their power: it will become more difficult to influence Russia, jeopardizing by jeopardizing access to Western European markets.
At the most tense moment, Warsaw did not stagnate before comparing the Northern Flote with the new “Hermo-Soviet Pact”, hinting at an alliance between Hitler and Stalin with the aim of occupying Poland in 1939.
This means that the issue is politically sensible.
Supporting this Russian project, Western Europe seeks greater security of its supplies.
But at the cost of depleting Europe of energy, because the project has created a gap between Eastern and Western Europe.
In less than a five-five years, in less than five years to achieve its understanding of a direct alliance between Russia and rich Western countries that consume large volumes of gas and whose own reserves are at an outcome.
“This gas pipeline is part of cooperation with Russia, it is a new artery that organically binds us,” François Fillon said, revealing a gas pipeline, demonstrating the extent to which large gas contracts are important both politically and economically.
All of this explains the wide smiling on the persons of the heads of Gazprom, who were present in a large number in Lyubin, the point of arrival of gas.
The construction of this gastrointestinal is also a technical feat.
The undersea pipeline is made of steel enclosed inconcre to protect it from the anchors of ships.
It lies at the bottom of the sea, at an average depth of 200 meter.
In order to build it, it was necessary to bypass the mine fields that remained from the Second World War.
“The hundred had to be removed or destroyed as a precaution,” said Jons Müller, a spokeswoman for Nord Potok.
It was also necessary to take a lot of steps to protect fauna and flora.
The Pipe Pipeline is a long metal serpent weighing 242 Eiffel turrets, without turmoil along its entire length, without valves and without service stations.
The control platform was planned in the region of Sweden, but the project managers abandoned it, because Sweden was not enthusiastic that the Russian state-owned company would permanently settle off its coast.
“In the event of an accident, we will block the gas flow in less than a minute,” says Jens Müller.
So, in the event of a dilapidation, the gas contained in the gas pipeline will go into the air.
But this seems uncomfortable to the designers, who have designed seams, designed only once every 100 000 years.
The condition of the gas pipeline will be carried out by an underwater robot that pulls the ship for external observation, as well as an apparatus circulating inside the gas pipeline.
Cygar-shaped device is inserted inside the pipeline with a diameter of 1 meter and is pushed forward with a flow of gas.
Upon arrival after 3 full days of travel at a speed of 3 meter per second, it gives accurate information about any deformation of the metal.
The gas pipeline has been designed to work for a period of 50 years unnecessarily needed the slightest repair.
Circulation of gas is carried out only due to its pressure.
It is 200 bar when departing and 100 bar upon arrival.
Five companies have joined forces to carry out this project.
The leader remains Gazprom, which owns 51% of the capital.
The rest are the German companies E.ON and BASF (15.5% each), the Dutch Gasunie and the French GDF Suez (9 per cent each).
These five companies have established a joint venture, called the Northern Flote, which was tasked to build and operate a gas pipeline.
Its headquarters are located in Tsuga in Switzerland, where taxation is especially favorable.
Then Gazprom leased this company for twenty years with the possibility of extending the entire volume of gas transportation.
“Gazprom will pay for a full volume, no matter how much gas will actually be transported,” says Jens Müller.
Financing of the construction of the gas pipeline was ensured by 30 per cent by shareholders and 70% of bank loans.
The total cost of the works will be 7.4 thousand million euros for two pipelines.
GDF Suez investments will be about 240 million.
But the minority shareholders are confident that they will recognize their costs, because Gazprom takes all the risks.
The gas pipeline comes out of the Baltic Sea in Lubmin on the beast, planted with convoy trees.
Veneers 4.5 meter with a height of forming an outdated gas terminal.
Sensors measure the pressure, the temperature and the specific characteristics of the gas before pumping it into German gas pipelines.
Since last Tuesday the terminal receives one million cubic meter of gas every hour.
At full capacity, this will be 3 million per hour, and in 2012 6 million.
Moleskine Blockade
Moleskine, created by the Italian company fifteen years ago, will return the taste for the letter.
He has an fragrance of the adventures, the hours spent behind the letter by a candid.
Moleskine note is easily recognizable on a rectangular black cub, by rubbish, along the yellow-and-and-and-wheetched pages, as if turned yellow over time.
But Moleskine’s notebook like we know it today was born in 1997.
The Italian company Modo, located in Milan, decided to put on the sale of designer notebooks.
Maria Sebegondi, the then consultant of the company, took responsibility for the launch of a new product.
The notebook is inspired by an old-fashioned technique, a polished cotton cloth, used, for example, to cover the benches of benches.
It is claimed that this type of notebook is highly appreciated by writers and travelers.
“Moleskine brought into line with today’s taste of an old and forgotten vein, which was a cult for avant-garde artists until the twentieth century,” said Maria Sebegondi, who has since become the management brand in Modo Modo.
Succeed has come.
From 2006 to 2010, sales increased by 25 per cent and reached 12.7 million.
We went far from the production of the first years, when only 3000 notebooks were produced.
Moleskine has crossed the borders of Italy and is exported to 70 countries, from France to the United States.
It is difficult to establish the profile of a typical buyer, because the notebook equally attracts a businesswoman, a student and a person of a free profession.
Moleskine buyers are cosmopolit, have broad views and are educated.
A small Italian company, which at the beginning had only 12 employees, now has 100 and two offices: one in Milan, and the other in New York.
It distributes its notebooks in Fnac bookstores, shops in small towns centers and was able to gain wide popularity.
"We followed the spirit of the time and this new need for a letter, despite the appearance of e-mail," explains Maria Sebregondi.
This characteristic cultural trait accompanies Moleskine's development; the brand recently organized the Okolean Path exhibition, where architects and artists have exhibited their own notebooks.
In August, he also opened the covers with a leopard drawing on Locarno.
Taking advantage of their success and cultural aura, Moleskine diversified its products, which now include bags, pens, computer bags. The brand includes all kinds of support.
In the autumn of 2006, Modo Modo was bought by SG Capital Europe, now Syntegra Capital, which inscribing a new page in Moleskine’s history.
Why is Unemployment for Disabled Huscepting Unemployment?
Approximately 19% of the disabled are looking for a job.
Week of Disabled Employment is Beginning Today.
